  /* What each view is ABOUT, in one line.

     The line used to be "Overview · 38 Cities · 134 Projects", and it did
     two jobs badly. It repeated the view's name inside its own
     description, so the path band read "Innovation" over "Innovation-as-a
     Service · Digital Twins" — two copies of one word where the reader
     expected a name and a description. And the figures it carried were the
     view's own headline numbers: the Overview's h1 reads "38 cities. What
     changed?" and a stat pair further down the same view reads 38 and 134,
     so the chrome said "38 · 134" a third time on the same screen.

     So the description says what is IN the view, and it never repeats the
     name it describes. It is said once per view: in the strapline in the
     plate bar for the view the reader is in, and under each destination
     in the path band.

     The numbers are the site's own and do not move: 38 cities, 134
     projects, 378 appendix rows, 6 focus areas, 32 outlines, 10 meetings,
     62 documents, 40 archived items. They belong to the views that state
     them, in context. */
